  "title": "China Bars Bloomberg Reporter from Trump-Xi Meet Amid Reporting on Nvidia",
  "summary": "China bars Bloomberg reporter Annmarie Hordern from a key trilateral meeting between President Donald Trump, Chinese leader Xi Jinping, and Russian President Vladimir Putin in Shenzhen, China, after she asked Trump about the alleged extramarital affair with former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang. The reporter was excluded from the event, reportedly as a retribution for her questioning the leader during a Trump meeting.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Annmarie Hordern was barred from the trilateral meeting in Shenzhen, China, after she asked a question about Jensen Huang's alleged extramarital affair with a Chinese spy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reporter was excluded from the event, and the White House stated the official requested anonymity due to the sensitivity of the issue.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "China denied the reporter's exclusion, claiming it was a response to the question and not an act of retaliation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
